        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nuclear Deterrence",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    DETERRENCE LOGIC                                  |\n|                                                                      |\n|  ACTOR A (potential attacker)                                        |\n|  Expected benefit of attack = pV - (1-p) × Punishment                |\n|                                                                      |\n|  p    = probability of attack succeeding                             |\n|  V    = value of objective                                           |\n|  Punishment = what you suffer in retaliation                         |\n|                                                                      |\n|  DETER BY DENIAL: make p small (attack can't succeed)                |\n|  DETER BY PUNISHMENT: make Punishment massive (retaliation certain)  |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Nuclear deterrence primarily works through punishment               |\n|  MAD = Punishment → infinity → expected value always negative        |\n|                                                                      |\n|  CREDIBILITY PROBLEM:                                                |\n|  Punishment must be BELIEVED to matter                               |\n|  If attacker doubts you'll retaliate → deterrence fails              |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
